breaking_changes.Adaptation_method:
Declare expected arguments explicitly using `.argument()` to handle variable input, or re-enable the previous lenient behavior by calling `.allowExcessArguments(true)`. Example:

Before:
```js
program.option('-p, --port <number>', 'port number');
program.action((options) => {
  console.log(program.args);
});
```

After (recommended):
```js
program.option('-p, --port <number>', 'port number');
program.argument('[args...]', 'remote command and arguments');
program.action((args, options) => {
  console.log(args);
});
```

Or (for backward compatibility):
```js
program.option('-p, --port <number>', 'port number');
program.allowExcessArguments(true);
program.action((options) => {
  console.log(program.args);
});
```

Ensure all option flags use valid syntax:

- For multi-character short flags (e.g., `-ab`), either split them into individual flags or define them intentionally as a combined flag.
- For dual long flags (e.g., `--es --ecmascript`), ensure you are using Commander v13.1.0 or later.

Before (invalid in v13.0.0):
```js
new Option('-ab <value>', 'description') // throws error
program.option('--es --ecmascript', 'enable ECMAScript');
```

After (valid):
```js
// Use separate short flags
program.option('-a', 'enable feature A');
program.option('-b <value>', 'set value for B');

// Or use a combined short flag if intended
program.option('-ab <value>', 'combined flag');

// Dual long flags are supported in v13.1+
program.option('--es --ecmascript', 'enable ECMAScript');
```

Avoid multiple calls to `.parse()` when `storeOptionsAsProperties: true`, or disable the option and access parsed values via `.opts()`. Example:

Before:
```js
program.storeOptionsAsProperties(true);
program.parse(process.argv);
program.parse(['--port', '3000']); // throws in v13
```

After:
```js
// Option 1: Use .opts() instead (recommended)
program.storeOptionsAsProperties(false);
program.option('--port <number>');
program.parse(process.argv);
const opts = program.opts();

// Option 2: Parse only once and avoid subsequent .parse() calls
program.parse(process.argv);
// Do not call .parse() again
```
